  "description": "Clean Architecture template — Infrastructure.Persistence core (provider-agnostic): AppDbContext base + AddAppDbContext/UseAppInterceptors registration, EfRepository (Ardalis.Specification), the 5-interceptor chain (EventDispatch, AuditableEntity, Audit.NET EF capture, SoftDelete, NoLock), NoLock read hints, PhenX bulk-insert contract, soft-delete query filters, EF Core OpenTelemetry contributor, and EfTransactionManager. Ships NO database provider — pair it with SU2.C15e.Infrastructure.Persistence.{SqlServer,Sqlite,PostgreSql,MySql,Oracle,Mongo}. The Dapper runtime moved to SU2.C15e.Infrastructure.Persistence.Dapper in 2.0.0 (ADR #043) — reference that package if you use IDbSession / AddDapper. Type namespaces stay SU2.C15e.Infrastructure.Data.* / .Persistence.Bulk / .Transactions for source compatibility. Numeronym `C15e` = CleanArchitecture. Generation 2026 series. See docs/plans/infrastructure-persistence-package-split-redesign.md.",
